WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
A crowd gathers round a metal cylinder.

2
00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:05.780
The lid turns, slowly.

3
00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:08.060
They expect a man to climb out.

4
00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:12.050
Instead, something the
size of a bear rises.

5
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:17.160
"Those who have never seen a living Martian
can scarcely imagine the strange horror

6
00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:19.040
of its appearance."

7
00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:21.660
Now put a human outline beside it.

8
00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:24.440
Look at the two shapes, side by side.

9
00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:27.470
The Martians are written to horrify us.

10
00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:30.300
So why do they look like our future?

11
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:33.420
In this mission, you'll take
apart that first description,

12
00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:35.670
and the Greek myth inside it.

13
00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:40.560
You'll look inside their machines, and
find that the Martians are "heads—merely

14
00:00:40.610 --> 00:00:41.760
heads".

15
00:00:41.810 --> 00:00:45.710
And you'll meet a strange
prediction from 1893.

16
00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:50.040
Your mission: explain why these
monsters look like our future.
